WEBVTT

00:18:27.643 --> 00:18:31.607
suddenly, something really weirdly cosmic
happens, and there's an opening,

00:18:31.631 --> 00:18:35.214
and now you're on the jet stream,
and it's flowing and you're in that space,

00:18:35.238 --> 00:18:37.819
and that's magic, and it's worth
working very hard for.

00:18:37.843 --> 00:18:40.111
But you don't get it for free.

00:18:41.662 --> 00:18:44.238
CA: Liz, I'd love to go back
and explore a little more

00:18:44.262 --> 00:18:48.634
this notion of this world in which there
are creative people who are sitting there,

00:18:48.658 --> 00:18:50.340
hoping for a moment of inspiration,

00:18:50.364 --> 00:18:53.305
and then there's this universe of ideas.

00:18:53.329 --> 00:18:56.489
Now, you describe them as these entities
that are sort of conscious

00:18:56.513 --> 00:18:58.987
and waiting for their path
through a human mind

00:18:59.011 --> 00:19:01.097
and out into the public sphere.